   184	    - The background is azure (8), with 1-cell-thick bars made from blue (1) and red (2) cells attached to alternating side walls.
   185	    - Exactly one green (3) pixel sits on a border and marks the route's start.
   186	
   187	    Rule:
   188	    - Each bar's safety radius is its red-cell count, i.e. total bar length minus blue-cell count, so bars with more blue allow a tighter pass.
   189	    - That radius is measured with Chebyshev distance, so every bar creates a square-cornered forbidden halo rather than a Manhattan diamond.
   190	    - The path uses orthogonal steps to reach the opposite edge, and all blue bar cells turn red in the output.
